              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Rectangles are similar if the ratio of their corresponding sides is same. First measure length and width of each rectangle (A, B, C, D, E) using scale. Calculate the ratio of length and width of each rectangle. Compare the ratios. If ratios are same then the rectangles are similar."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.409,
            0.847,
            0.484
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Look at the following rectangle. Can you draw a smaller rectangle and a bigger rectangle with the same width to height ratio in your notebooks? Compare your rectangles with your classmates’ drawings."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.484,
            0.847,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Are all of them the same? If they are different from yours, can you think why? Are they wrong?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.375,
            0.53,
            0.59,
